# solid_sdd

This project uses solid_sdd for machine-checkable Spec-Driven Development.

## Where to start

- Multi-criterion change (spans several acceptance criteria) → **`solidsdd-run`**
- Single known slice (one clear acceptance criterion) → **`solidsdd-loop`**
- Framing is ambiguous before either → **`solidsdd-grill`** (optional, conditional)
- A human-readable snapshot of a change → **`solidsdd-report`** (manual only, not part of `solidsdd-run`)

Read the skill you are about to invoke for procedure; do not infer procedure from this file, and do not thin or rewrite its artifacts (Change Context, ChangeBrief, WorkPlan, ApplicationPlan, CritiqueReport, VerificationReport, knowledge-harvest.json) in the parent.

## Non-negotiable

Never mark a change `done`, or a slice complete, while a required check, critique, or human gate is unresolved.
